You should also make sure that before you download, you’ve looked through our checklist of all things to prevent things from going wrong and protecting yourself if they’re. iOS 9 brings new features, including a much smarter personal assistant, and huge new productivity features for the iPad, as well as changes that accelerate and repair the operating system.
Rosberg's only motto: Full attack
Nico Rosberg knows only one most in the fight for the World Championship title in Formula 1 against his clearly leading Mercedes team-mate Lewis Hamilton: "Full attack."
The World Cup runner-up emphasized before the start to the decisive seven overseas races "that I have nothing left to lose."
53 points separate the runner-up world champion ahead of the night race in Singapore this Sunday from defending champion and two-time champion Hamilton.
The Briton has already won seven of the previous twelve races of the season and is also attacking the floodlight Grand Prix in the city-state as the favorite.
In 2009 and last year the 30-year-old Briton won the race.
Whether the current smog in the city-state will have an impact on the Singapore Grand Prix is still unclear.
For days, a haze bell has been hanging over the city triggered by fires on the neighboring island of Sumatra.
Bad Kissinger Chess Club has a prominent member
The chess club "Chessfreunde Bad Kissingen", founded three months ago, has added another member in its ranks, thus increasing the number of members to 19 players.
The new member is the entrepreneur Paul Gauselmann, a passionate chess and tennis player who spent more than 40 times in Bad Kissingen.
Gauselmann is the recipient of the Bundesverdienstkreuz 1, class and honorary citizen of the cities of Espelkamp and Lübbecke.
Gauselmann supported the chess club in Bad Kissingen with a donation received by Chairman Alfred Klein.
Thus, it is possible to accept chess players who are unable to raise the membership fee.
Youth work and talent search are also to be promoted.
Gauselmann hopes that the membership in the chess club and also friendly contact with the tennis club "Rot-Weiß" will be seen as an expression of his attachment to the spa town.
Neighbourhood office seeks direct contact
Saludis and the Altenzentrum Antonistift teamed up under the mangle of the social foundation and opened a new contact point at Graf-Stauffenberg-Platz.
In addition to consultations, you can also participate in courses there.
The social foundation pulls it down from the mountain to the city center.
More specifically to Graf-Stauffenberg-Platz.
A new district office was recently opened there.
Here, directly next to the shopping market, senior citizens and advice seekers now receive information on questions such as long-term care insurance or health and nursing care funds.
For years we have noticed with our outpatient nursing service that caring relatives are often left alone.
There are an infinite number of questions.
"Not infrequently, many services of the coffers are not used, because the complexity of the insurance companies is hardly understood anymore," explained the new landlord Jutta Weigand, who is also responsible for the Antonistift and the Bürgerspital as well as for the outpatient service "Amadeus".
In addition to the consultations, the new district office also offers prevention, health courses and wellness.
For this purpose, the saludis was taken on board.
Therefore, you can take advantage of additional offers such as fall prevention, memory training or physiotherapeutic treatment.
The offers from the senior center and the Saludis complement each other in an ideal way.
Saludis stands for prevention, prevention and rehab.
"The senior center for care and care," described Heike Riedel, managing director of Saludis.
Both managing directors see the reason for the opening of the new district office in the city centre, especially in demographic change.
Because this makes a good decentralized infrastructure in the individual districts of Bamberg indispensable in the future.
In addition, according to mayor Wolfgang Metzner (SPD) at the inauguration celebrations, the district office is also dedicated to solitude in old age: "There are numerous events and offers on the program and these invite to a regular social gathering".
In this way, the Social Foundation makes a great contribution to ensuring that senior citizens can live as independently and well as possible in their familiar environment.
The district office is open Monday, Wednesday and Friday from 9 a.m. to 2 p.m., Tuesday and Thursday from 4 p.m. to 6 p.m. and Saturdays from 10 a.m. to 12 p.m.
Eintracht Bamberg against Würzburger Kickers on October 6
Now it is official: After the date for the game FC Eintracht Bamberg had not yet been set against the third league Würzburger Kickers due to renovation work at the Fuchsparkstadion, October 6 has now been determined as the date.
The encounter of FC Eintracht Bamberg in the eighth final of the Bavarian Football Totokal against the third division FC Würzburg Kickers has now been definitively terminated.
It will take place on Tuesday, October 6, at 7 p.m. at Bamberg's Fuchsparkstadion.
"We are happy that we now know when the game will take place, now we have planning security," according to FCE team manager Karlheinz Hümmer, who is also pointing to the ticket pre-sale now launched.
It's something special for our team to play against a third-tier club.
We therefore hope for numerous spectators, and not without reason, because floodlight games have a special appeal.
FC Eintracht Bamberg moved into the round of the last 16 teams in 2010 through victories at district league 1. FC Oberhaid (3:1) and at home against the regional league 1. FC Schweinfurt 05 (3:2).
The winner of the competition will receive 5000 euros and qualifies for the first round of the DFB Club Cup 2016/2017.
Defending champion is third-league relegated SpVgg Unterhaching.
Viennese architect Karl Mang dies at 92
Karl Mang, one of the doyens of Viennese architecture, has died.
He died on September 5 at the age of 92, as the Künstlerhaus announced on Tuesday.
With Mang, the Künstlerhaus lost an honorary member and at the same time "one of the most important architects of the second half of the 20th century in Vienna," as it said in the broadcast.
Born in 1922 in Vienna, Mang graduated with Friedrich Lehmann during and after the Second World World Worship at the Technical University in Vienna.
Since 1952 he worked as a freelance architect, but also worked as a teacher, writer and head of the institute.
From 1972 to 1989 he was president of the Austrian Institute of Design.
In the 1980s he was commissioned with the establishment of the treasury in the Viennese Hofburg and the conversion of the Lobkowitz Palace into the Austrian Theatre Museum.
